     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu found an old coin in the field and showed it to her teacher.\n\"Coins tell us about the past,\" he said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "archaeology",
     "inscription",
     "source"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Historians use sources to learn about the past. Archaeological sources are objects found in the ground such as coins, tools, pots, bones and buildings.\nLiterary sources are written records such as books, inscriptions and manuscripts.\nArchaeologists dig carefully and study layers to date objects. We should protect old monuments."
    }
